        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): remove no-op timer leak in realtime talk mark handler",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `scheduleMarkAck()` method in `realtime-talk-gateway-relay.ts` creates a `window.setTimeout(() => {}, delayMs)` timer that does nothing — the callback is empty and the return value (timer ID) is discarded. This is a timer leak: every relay mark event creates an unreferenced timer that sits in memory until it fires on an empty callback.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe mark event from the gateway relay does not require client-side acknowledgment — the relay handles it automatically. The no-op timer was either dead code left from an earlier design or an incomplete feature stub. Keeping it in the hot path wastes timer slots and contributes to memory pressure during prolonged realtime-talk sessions.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Eliminates timer resource leaks during realtime voice sessions\n- Reduces unnecessary runtime overhead from no-op timeout creation\n- No user-visible behavior change — mark events continue to be handled as a no-op\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Test output\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/pages/chat/realtime-talk-gateway-relay.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  19 passed (19)\n   Start at  08:37:11\n   Duration  1.51s\n```\n\n### Lint/format/typecheck\n\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check`: All matched files use the correct format\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs`: No lint errors\n- `pnpm tsgo`: No type errors\n- `git diff --check`: PASSED\n\n### Before/After\n\n**Before**: Each relay mark event created `window.setTimeout(() => {}, delayMs)` with a discarded timer ID, leaking a timer handle per event.\n\n**After**: The `scheduleMarkAck` method is removed entirely. The `case \"mark\"` handler returns early with a comment explaining that the relay handles acknowledgment automatically.\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nOpenClaw starts successfully with the patched code:\n\n```\n$ pnpm openclaw --version\n[openclaw] Building TypeScript (dist is stale: config_newer - config newer than build stamp).\n[openclaw] Building bundled plugin assets.\n[... build completes ...]\n```\n\nThe gateway relay transport continues to handle all events (audio, transcript, toolCall, toolResult, close) as before — only the no-op timer was removed.",
        "branch": "fix/realtime-talk-gateway-relay-timer-leak",
